WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:03.233
[music]

2
00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:08.566
[Instructor] All right, so we have
a really good-looking game now,

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.433
with all the cool mechanics,
and animation set up properly,

4
00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:14.966
and now we're going to add
the finishing touches

5
00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:17.233
when we Collide with that Obstacle,

6
00:00:17.866 --> 00:00:20.066
to create a really cool
smoke effect.

7
00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:23.100
So, to do that,
we're actually going to learn

8
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.000
how to use Particle effects.

9
00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:27.900
Now, if you go into your Assets,

10
00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:30.033
under the Course Library,

11
00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.066
there's actually a Particles Folder.

12
00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:35.100
And if you expand
the "Particles" Folder,

13
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.100
you can see there's "FX_DirtSplatter,"

14
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.600
and Smoke Explosion.

15
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.566
So, we're going to take
this "FX_Explosion_Smoke,"

16
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.700
and drag it into our Hierarchy,

17
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.133
and then you can see
it creates this really cool puff

18
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:54.600
when we place it, and you can see
there's actually a little section

19
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.500
down in the bottom right
of our Scene,

20
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.500
we'll make that a little bigger,

21
00:00:59.766 --> 00:01:03.400
and in this Menu you can
actually Play, Restart, or Stop

22
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.766
the animation of our Particle effect.

23
00:01:05.766 --> 00:01:08.433
So if we Play, and we can Restart,

24
00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:10.433
and we can Restart as much as we want,

25
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:12.566
and we can Stop it,
and we can Play,

26
00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.800
so this is just a kind of cool way
to see the Effects,

27
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.200
and how they work. Now, another cool
thing about our Particle System

28
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.800
is that there's a whole bunch
of options

29
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.366
that you can actually change
on the Particle System,

30
00:01:24.733 --> 00:01:27.066
to be able to make it
do different things,

31
00:01:27.866 --> 00:01:30.166
so you can actually go,
and change how fast

32
00:01:30.166 --> 00:01:33.766
the actual Particles
move over their lifetime,

33
00:01:33.766 --> 00:01:36.566
so if we set the Speed
to be ten times as fast,

34
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.033
should move even faster than
before.

35
00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.533
Yeah, so it's like a big phh!
That's actually kind of cool,

36
00:01:42.533 --> 00:01:44.533
I'm going to leave that.

37
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.733
So we'll Stop that. So it's pretty cool,
we can set different options, too,

38
00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:53.000
that we want, so we can change
the colors if we wanted to,

39
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.400
we could change how they
actually expand,

40
00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.700
all these other different options.
Actually, you know what?

41
00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.966
I'm going to set the Speed back
to be 2.

42
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.766
So, there's all these different
ways you can Play around

43
00:02:03.766 --> 00:02:06.233
with Particle Effects, honestly,
you could do 100

44
00:02:06.233 --> 00:02:08.866
different things with them.
I'm not going to go too crazy,

45
00:02:08.866 --> 00:02:11.866
just because the base effect
is really good for now,

46
00:02:11.866 --> 00:02:13.900
so we're just going to use it.

47
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.900
One thing that you want
to be really careful of though,

48
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:18.933
with your Particle Effects, 
is if you open

49
00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:21.466
up the Particle System Menu,

50
00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.000
you can actually see
there's a "Play On Awake*,"

51
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.333
and if we set that to true, that would
immediately create a huge puff of smoke

52
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:31.166
when the game starts. That's not
exactly what we want to happen,

53
00:02:31.166 --> 00:02:33.466
that's not the kind of effect
that we're trying to create,

54
00:02:33.533 --> 00:02:36.766
unless this character were a magician,
then that would make a lot more sense.

55
00:02:36.766 --> 00:02:39.000
So we'll uncheck
the Play On Awake*.

56
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.133
So now,
one thing that we're going to do

57
00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:43.466
is actually put

58
00:02:43.466 --> 00:02:46.666
this FX_Explosion_Smoke
underneath our Player,

59
00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:50.800
as a "Nested" or a "Child" Object.

60
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.966
So that means that it's
an Object that is attached

61
00:02:54.233 --> 00:02:58.400
to another Object, so it
belongs as part of that Object.

62
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:02.100
So you can actually see Player,
you can see the character,

63
00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.000
and you can see the actual
legs that control it.

64
00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:09.366
If we drag
in our FX_Explosion_Smoke on Player,

65
00:03:09.366 --> 00:03:11.533
you can see now, that Player

66
00:03:11.533 --> 00:03:15.000
has a smoke explosion
effect attached to it.

67
00:03:16.566 --> 00:03:19.666
And now, what we can
actually do is when we Play,

68
00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:23.066
we can actually move
our Particle effect around, so,

69
00:03:23.566 --> 00:03:26.966
if we Restart,
see it starts kind of high...

70
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.000
so we can actually...

71
00:03:33.466 --> 00:03:36.466
go, and maybe,
let's just the Y down to 0,

72
00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:38.366
so it's at the bottom
of the Player's feet.

73
00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.566
And then we Restart, and there you go,
and now it's closer to the Ground,

74
00:03:42.566 --> 00:03:44.566
maybe we'll make it
a little bit higher.

75
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.533
Something like, not too high, 0.5,
I think is good.

76
00:03:50.466 --> 00:03:53.100
And then Play, cool, 
so that's a pretty good position.

77
00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.000
So, if you watch at the bottom,

78
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.000
it's like a puff of smoke,

79
00:03:58.033 --> 00:04:01.300
and it creates a really cool effect.
So, now what you're going to do

80
00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.933
is you're going to go
into your Assets Folder,

81
00:04:04.233 --> 00:04:07.200
in your Course Library,
go to the Particles Folder,

82
00:04:07.666 --> 00:04:09.766
take the FX_Explosion_Smoke,

83
00:04:09.766 --> 00:04:11.633
and you're actually
going to drag

84
00:04:11.633 --> 00:04:14.066
it directly onto the Player,

85
00:04:14.066 --> 00:04:16.200
so that then it becomes
a Child Object

86
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.200
of that Player.

87
00:04:18.433 --> 00:04:20.500
And then you can go,
and fiddle around

88
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.333
with the FX_Explosion_Smoke

89
00:04:22.866 --> 00:04:24.733
setting its position,

90
00:04:24.733 --> 00:04:27.100
maybe you want to make
it on the head for some reason,

91
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.600
you can go, and mess around
with some of the settings,

92
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.433
but just don't go too wild with it.

93
00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.466
And then you're good to go.
Now, it's your turn.

94
00:04:38.266 --> 00:04:40.100
[music]
